Prepare pods without slowing connected exec

Allow exec to create missing pods with confirmation or --create,
restart stopped pods, and reconnect disconnected pods through enter's
launch path. Keep stdin untouched until execution is accepted and send
launch progress to stderr so preparation cannot corrupt command input
or output.

Preserve the single-request connected path. Only a daemon response
proving that no command was forwarded permits preparation and another
attempt; transport failures and ambiguous server errors still cannot
replay commands. Wait for connection readiness after launch before
starting the command.

Cover creation consent, terminal restoration, piped input, clean stdout,
restart, reconnection, and the connected command's single RPC in
integration tests.
